# Plan phase (`y-agt-plan-phase`)

Run this rule **before** `CreatePlan` or writing a plan file. Complete this phase first, then choose a [plan document approach](#12-plan-document-approach-mandatory-askquestion) and call **`CreatePlan`** per [`y-agt-plan-guidelines.mdc`](y-agt-plan-guidelines.mdc).

**Use when** the user asks to plan, enters plan mode, invokes **`/y-agt-plan`**, or **`@y-agt-plan-phase`**.

Plans: follow [`y-agt-workspace.mdc`](y-agt-workspace.mdc) — not `cursor_workspace/`.

---

## Pipeline (follow in order)

Skip steps the user already answered in the same thread.

### 1. AskQuestion availability

Every decision below must use **`AskQuestion`** — follow the mandatory gate pattern in [`y-git-commits.mdc`](../git/y-git-commits.mdc) § AskQuestion gates (no chat-only confirmation).

**If `AskQuestion` is unavailable:** tell the user plainly that planning needs structured confirmations. Ask them to **continue without gates** or **stop**. Do **not** silently skip ticket, approach, or E2E questions.

### 2. Jira ticket key

If the user did not provide a ticket key (e.g. `VAP-1234`), **`AskQuestion`** before research. Allow **`other`** = no ticket → record under plan **`## Open questions`**.

### 3. Fetch context

When a key exists:

- **Jira** — workspace **`jira-workflow`** rule: `getJiraIssue` with `contentFormat: "markdown"`; read **all** comments and linked issue references.
- **GitHub** — `gh` only when the ticket links PRs/branches or implementation context needs it.
- **Confluence** — Atlassian MCP only when the ticket links a page or the user points to a spec.
- **Repo artifacts** — scan `docs/<KEY>/`, RFC paths, and test docs mentioned in the ticket or comments.

Summarize findings briefly in chat before drafting the plan.

### 4. Clarify ticket

- **Vague or contradictory description** — apply [`y-team-task-refinement.mdc`](../team/y-team-task-refinement.mdc) **§ step 4 only** (vagueness check). **`AskQuestion`** on remaining gaps.
- **Missing or thin AC** — [`y-agt-task-context.mdc`](y-agt-task-context.mdc) (AC structure).
- **Thin overall context** — [`y-agt-task-context.mdc`](y-agt-task-context.mdc) § When ticket context is thin.

Do **not** run the full refinement pipeline (create ticket, steps 1–8) — the ticket already exists.

### 5. Solution approach (mandatory AskQuestion)

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Minimal and efficient** (default) | Smallest correct change; no drive-by refactors |
| **Thorough / production-grade** | Deeper fix, broader hardening, more investigation |
| **Quick fix** | Fast patch; limited root-cause analysis |
| **`other`** | User describes a different bar |

Record the choice in the plan — **Rules approach:** **`## Constraints`** bullet **Solution approach**. **Cursor approach:** include the same fact in the plan body where it fits (no fixed section required).

### 6. Engineering guardrails

Capture in the plan for both approaches:

- **No side effects** — do not change unrelated code paths.
- **No regressions** — preserve behavior outside the fix scope.
- **No unrelated flow breaks** — unless the ticket requires fixing them.
- **No over-engineering** — no premature abstractions or “while we’re here” refactors.

**Rules approach:** record under **`## Constraints`**. **Cursor approach:** weave into the plan body (e.g. approach or risks) — no mandatory **Constraints** section.

### 7. E2E / testing scope (mandatory AskQuestion)

| Option | Plan behavior |
|--------|----------------|
| **No E2E in this plan** | Omit E2E sub-tasks; note under **Out of scope** |
| **E2E later** | Defer to **`## Open questions`** or **Out of scope** |
| **Not needed** | State why (e.g. docs-only) |
| **E2E in this plan** | Add optional plan **`## Testing`** with sub-tasks that **link** to rules below — no runbook copy |

Record choice in the plan — **Rules approach:** **`## Constraints`** bullet **Testing scope**. **Cursor approach:** state testing scope in the plan body (e.g. near goals or implementation notes).

**When E2E in this plan** and generative-search rules are installed, sub-tasks cite (in order):

1. `y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-testing-criteria.mdc`
2. `y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-test-cases.mdc`
3. `y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e.mdc` (→ ResiRoo or PMRoo sub-rule as needed)
4. `y-generative-search-rules/insight/y-ins-e2e-report.mdc`

Optional when relevant: `y-tst-unit-of-code`, `y-tst-test-case` ([`y-rules/test/y-tst-test-case.mdc`](../test/y-tst-test-case.mdc)), marketplace/resiroo/pmroo payload rules.

For repos without generative-search rules, plan high-level testing only (pytest, manual QA).

### 8. Ruff format/lint in plan todos (AskQuestion when Python)

When the plan includes **Python code changes**, or the repo has **Ruff** configured (`pyproject.toml`, `ruff.toml`, Makefile, pre-commit), **`AskQuestion`**:

| Option | Plan behavior |
|--------|----------------|
| **Yes — include Ruff todos** (default) | Add **`ruff format`** and **`ruff check`** to plan **YAML `todos`** and to implementation sub-tasks (Rules approach). Run on touched Python paths before handoff/PR. |
| **No** | Omit Ruff todos; note briefly in **Out of scope** or plan body if the user declined. |

**Default:** **Yes** — pre-select **Yes** in **`AskQuestion`** when the tool allows a default.

Skip when the plan is **non-Python only** (docs-only, config outside Python, no Ruff in repo).

**Todo text (example):** `Run ruff format and ruff check on changed Python files; fix findings before PR`

Use the repo’s usual invocation (`ruff`, `uv run ruff`, `make lint`, etc.) in the sub-task detail when known.

### 9. Code docs in plan todos (AskQuestion when Python API)

When the plan includes **new or changed Python public API** (modules, classes, functions, methods callers use), **`AskQuestion`**:

| Option | Plan behavior |
|--------|----------------|
| **Yes — include code-docs todos** (default) | Add docstrings for new/changed public members **while implementing** per [`y-dev-code-docs.mdc`](../dev/y-dev-code-docs.mdc). Include YAML `todos` and implementation sub-tasks — same PR as the code, not a deferred doc-only pass. |
| **No** | Omit code-docs todos; note briefly in **Out of scope** if the user declined. |

**Default:** **Yes** — pre-select **Yes** in **`AskQuestion`** when the tool allows a default.

Skip when the plan is **non-Python**, **docs-only**, or **no public API changes** (internal refactor with unchanged contracts).

**Todo text (example):** `Document new/changed public Python API per y-dev-code-docs while implementing`

Dedicated doc-only sessions use **`/y-dev-code-docs`** — do not substitute that full gated workflow for this plan todo.

### 10. RFC (conditional)

If **Thorough / production-grade** and design is still unclear: add a plan sub-task — **Read and follow [`y-dev-rfc.mdc`](../dev/y-dev-rfc.mdc)**. Do **not** inline the RFC workflow here.

### 11. Branch (optional note only)

If the plan mentions a branch, cite [`y-git-branch-name.mdc`](../git/y-git-branch-name.mdc). Do **not** run `git checkout` during planning.

### 12. Plan document approach (mandatory AskQuestion)

After steps 1–11 (or explicit skips), **`AskQuestion`** how to shape the **plan document** (content and structure only — steps 2–11 context still applies to both):

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Cursor approach** (default when user wants speed) | Cursor chooses sections and depth from ticket context, repo, and phase answers. Does **not** require the full rules section catalog. |
| **Rules approach** | Full structure per [`y-agt-plan-guidelines.mdc`](y-agt-plan-guidelines.mdc) — **Rules path** section order. |
| **`other`** | User describes a hybrid (e.g. rules sub-tasks but skip Product perspective). |

Skip this gate only when the user **already chose** the same option in the same thread.

**Both paths** must still follow guidelines **Common to all plans** (versioning, **`## Goals`**, **`## Out of scope`**, storage, YAML frontmatter).

### 13. Diagrams (AskQuestion when reasonable)

When the task involves **architecture, data flow, or multi-step runtime ordering**, **`AskQuestion`** whether to include **Mermaid diagram(s)** in the plan:

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Yes — include diagram(s)** | Add Mermaid where it clarifies (per guidelines Mermaid rules). |
| **No — text only** | No diagrams unless the user asks later. |
| **Let Cursor decide** | Include diagrams only if they clearly help; skip otherwise. |

If the plan is trivial (typo, single-file change, docs-only with no flow), **skip** this question.

### 14. Hand off

Only after steps 1–13 (or explicit skips): call **`CreatePlan`** using the approach from step 12 and diagram choice from step 13 (if asked), per [`y-agt-plan-guidelines.mdc`](y-agt-plan-guidelines.mdc).

**Post-implementation** (not this phase): PR and Local Tests Report → [`y-git-create-pr.mdc`](../git/y-git-create-pr.mdc). That rule requires the **full PR draft** (title + body code blocks) in chat **before** checklist or approve/edit **`AskQuestion`** gates.

---

## Do not

- Duplicate plan section catalogs, AC templates, Jira MCP tables, or E2E runbooks from other rules.
- Run full **`y-team-task-refinement`** on an existing ticket.
- Call **`CreatePlan`** before solution approach, E2E scope, Ruff todos choice (step 8 when applicable), code-docs todos choice (step 9 when applicable), plan document approach (step 12), or diagram choice (step 13 when applicable) are resolved or explicitly deferred.
